# What the backend build context excludes.
#
# The context is the repository root, because the API imports `ml`, `rag`,
# `llm` and `agent` and the retrieval layer indexes the project's own README
# files. So this file's job is to exclude everything that is *not* backend
# source — above all the frontend, which has its own image.
#
# Nothing here excludes a source file the build needs; the Dockerfile COPYs
# each package explicitly, so an over-broad rule would fail the build loudly
# rather than produce a subtly incomplete image.

# Version control and CI
.git/
.gitignore
.github/

# The dashboard has its own image and its own context.
frontend/

# Python caches and environments
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.so
.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
build/
dist/

# Test, lint and type-check caches
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
.tox/

# Local state that belongs in a volume, never in an image. The container
# builds its own retrieval index at start-up and writes experiment records to
# a volume; a developer's local copies of either must not be baked in.
rag/index/
ml/experiments/runs/
data/raw/
data/processed/

# Local configuration and anything secret. `.env.example` is documentation and
# is kept; a real `.env` never enters the context.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key

# Editor and OS noise
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.log

# Docker's own files
Dockerfile
*/Dockerfile
.dockerignore
docker-compose*.yml
